        "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
        "text": "<h2><span style=\"color: #1c5687;\"><span class=\"futura-bold\">Why is high blood pressure referred to as a ‘silent killer’?</span></span></h2>\n<p>The healthcare community often refers to hypertension as a ‘silent killer,’ and as harsh as the term sounds, it can become true if blood pressure goes unmonitored and unmanaged. Some patients with hypertension won’t have any visible symptoms to signal that they have a health problem.<sup>2</sup></p>\n<p>However, a different story is occurring inside the body. Untreated hypertension can cause damage to arteries – they can get clogged and in the most serious cases, the artery may burst.<sup>1</sup><br>\n</p>\n",
        "jcr:lastModified": "Tue Oct 15 2024 19:30:05 GMT+0000",
        "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
        "textIsRich": "true",
