        "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
        "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #1c5687;\">Are there different types of strokes?</span></span></h2>\n<p>Yes, there are several different types of strokes.<sup>3</sup> The one thing that they have in common is that they can be caused by high blood pressure.<sup>2</sup><br>\n</p>\n<ul>\n<li>An <b>ischemic stroke</b> occurs when there is a blockage of blood flow to the brain, usually caused by a blood clot or another substance such as plaque.<sup>3</sup><br>\n</li>\n<li>A <b>hemorrhagic stroke</b> occurs when a weakened blood vessel ruptures, causing blood to leak out of the vessel and into the surrounding brain tissue. One type of weakened blood vessel is an aneurysm. An aneurysm occurs when part of a blood vessel becomes weak and fills with blood, causing the vessel to balloon or bulge.<sup>3</sup></li>\n</ul>\n",
        "jcr:lastModified": "Mon Oct 21 2024 15:48:02 GMT+0000",
        "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
        "textIsRich": "true",
