        "gradientDirection": "left-to-right",
        "text": "<h2><span class=\"futura-bold\"><span style=\"color: #1c5687;\">How are strokes treated?</span></span></h2>\n<p>A stroke generally happens suddenly, and medical care needs to be administered as quickly as possible. To help keep this top of mind, we use the acronym <a href=\"/content/m/stroke-awareness/index.html\">B.E. F.A.S.T</a>. which identifies signs of a stroke. The best course of treatment depends on the type of stroke, the patient’s age, the severity of the stroke and other risk factors.</p>\n",
        "jcr:lastModified": "Wed Oct 23 2024 20:02:57 GMT+0000",
        "sling:resourceType": "stryker/components/content/text",
        "textIsRich": "true",
